    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 81.87 score makes him our most potent asset. Assuming a #2 spot in the lineup against Johnson, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a stellar 5.15 xERA matchup and a massive 14% boost from his dynamic platoon advantage. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (75.26) and **Andy Pages** (72.83) provide elite output; **Jackson Merrill** is a focal point despite the slight park penalty, as his strong platoon profile against the right-handed Ritchie overcomes the high-efficiency defensive unit he is facing. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.04) and **Jacob Wilson** (64.56) round out our premier starts, with the latter benefiting from favorable wind conditions that lift his offensive ceiling against Ray.\n\nOur toughest roster management decision involved the bench, where **Josh Jung** narrowly missed the cut with a 53.10 score. While **Josh Jung** maintains a respectable profile, he was relegated to the bench in favor of **Drake Baldwin** (57.95) and **Coby Mayo** (56.07), who both project for higher situational efficiency today. **Nasim Nunez** was also considered, but the combination of a difficult matchup against Luzardo and his lower spot in the order significantly suppressed his value compared to our starters. We are closely monitoring the lineup status for **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo**; while we have assumed their positions, any unexpected drop in the order or a late scratch could necessitate a pivot to our bench depth. We remain cautious with **Dominic Smith** (47.00), whose score is suppressed by a L/L platoon disadvantage against Peralta; he remains in the lineup to preserve our game caps, but he is at risk if his efficiency slips further as the game unfolds.",
